          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"version\":\"design_judgment_v1\",\"case_key\":\"ddd2f5a8191c1ae70b57ec33\",\"status\":\"scored\",\"units\":[{\"unit_id\":\"task_requirements\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Required: the reported No Service issue calls for customer identification and enough device troubleshooting to establish whether the agent can resolve it.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0004\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"}],\"rationale\":\"A defensible path identifies the customer, checks the service symptoms, addresses a discovered missing SIM, then checks SIM status again. A locked SIM is the decisive mandatory escalation condition; payment and APN repair are not required after it is established.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":2,\"tool_use\":2,\"information\":2}},{\"unit_id\":\"reference_001\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Selected conditional: the transfer action applies once the locked-SIM condition establishes that this issue cannot be solved with the available actions.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0314\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}],\"rationale\":\"Transfer requires recognizing the escalation condition, supplying an issue summary to the transfer tool, and then sending the prescribed transfer message. The reference action alone does not establish that transfer is appropriate without diagnosis.\",\"applicability\":\"selected_conditional\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":1,\"tool_use\":1,\"information\":1}}],\"dimensions\":{\"workload\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"The sufficient path has several routine stages: identify the customer, diagnose the phone, guide a SIM reseat when it is reported missing, establish the remaining locked-SIM condition, and transfer. An initial status check may also reveal airplane mode and warrant turning it off before the SIM diagnosis. The locked SIM is the decisive exit; exclude bill payment, line resumption, APN repair, and further service-restoration work afterward.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0206\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0207\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0011\"}]},\"reasoning\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"The agent must distinguish a missing SIM, which has a documented user fix, from a locked SIM, which requires escalation, while applying the restriction on transfers.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}]},\"tool_use\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"The path involves selecting a customer lookup, obtaining user-grounded device findings, binding those findings to troubleshooting guidance, and making the conditional transfer call. No complex transfer arguments are required.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0322\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0489\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0523\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0434\"}]},\"dependencies\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"Identification precedes technical support; the SIM must be checked and a missing-card finding addressed before a subsequent locked status establishes the decisive exit. A status-first path may also turn off airplane mode. Once the lock is established, transfer follows without paying the overdue bill or repairing the APN.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0206\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0207\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}]},\"information\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"The phone number is supplied, but device findings must be obtained rather than inferred from setup records. Rechecking SIM status after reseating resolves the relevant gap on this sufficient path.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0006\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0563\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0564\"}]}},\"overall_score\":50,\"intended_endpoint\":{\"description\":\"A valid human-agent transfer after discovering a locked SIM, with No Service unresolved; the prescribed transfer message follows the tool call. The completion requirement also specifies a no-service status, but does not prove an observed outcome.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0310\"}]},\"dependency_reasoning\":\"The chosen sufficient diagnostic order is customer lookup, device status and applicable airplane-mode guidance, SIM status, reseating if missing, then a renewed SIM check. The setup describes an unseated card and a separately locked SIM; the lock, once exposed, mandates escalation. Other diagnostic orders may be defensible, but the source does not require completing independently repairable billing or APN branches before a mandatory SIM-security exit.\",\"score_rationale\":\"Ratings of workload 2, reasoning 2, tool use 2, dependencies 2, and information 2 give 5 × 10 = 50. The score counts discovery and guidance needed to justify escalation, not every seeded fault or the reference transfer call in isolation.\",\"uncertainties\":[\"The supplied sources do not show the actual output of a SIM check after reseating; the sufficient path relies on the documented setup state and conditional SIM guidance, not an observed trace.\",\"Policy language to try all possible fixes before transfer is broad, while the SIM-specific rule directs escalation when the SIM is locked. The score treats that specific mandatory exit as decisive.\",\"The scenario names `get_status_bar` in an example, whereas the supplied user tool and troubleshooting guide name `check_status_bar`. This does not prevent scoring the diagnostic work.\"],\"source_quality_flags\":[\"Initialization and baseline records are judge-only design context, not facts already known to the task agent.\",\"The reference contains only a transfer call and is not a complete troubleshooting workflow.\",\"The completion requirement specifies an unresolved no-service state, while the user's preferred resolution is a signal; the intended valid endpoint is escalation rather than restored service.\"],\"unscorable_reason\":\"\"}",
          "type": "output_text",
          "logprobs": []
        }
